## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of multi-account setups and provider aliasing in modules. It also checks proper targeting and drift-free validation.

## Key Concepts
- Terraform providers and aliases
- Module-level provider configuration
- For_each environment handling
- Plan vs apply drift checks

## Code Example
```hcl
provider "aws" {
  alias = "dev"
  # credentials for dev account
}

provider "aws" {
  alias = "prod"
  # credentials for prod account
}

module "storage" {
  for_each = var.environments
  source   = "./modules/storage"
  providers = {
    aws = aws.dev
    aws.prod = aws.prod
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests environment isolation via provider aliases and per-env backends, plus CI gating for safe promotion to QA.

## Key Concepts
- Provider alias isolation
- Backend per environment
- CI gated plan/apply workflow

## Code Example
```hcl
terraform {
  required_version = ">= 1.4"

  backend "s3" {
    key    = "envs/qa/terraform.tfstate"
    region = "us-west-2"
  }
}

provider "aws" {
  alias = "qa"
  region = "us-west-2"
  assume_role {
    role_arn = "arn:aws:iam::ACCOUNT_QA:role/TerraformRole"
  }
}
```

